# Regenerate with: php spark clients:checksums
#
# These detect a STALE or CORRUPTED copy without executing anything -
# useful where a host forbids running downloaded code, which is exactly
# where require_version() cannot help you: calling it means importing
# the file you are trying to vet.
#
# They are NOT authentication. This file is served from the same origin
# as the files it describes, so a compromised relay could serve both a
# bad file and a matching hash. Treat it as an integrity check against
# staleness and transfer corruption, nothing more.
#
# Verify everything you downloaded:
#   sha256sum -c clients-SHA256SUMS
# Verify one file (portable; --ignore-missing needs coreutils 8.25+):
#   grep ' stringcup.py$' clients-SHA256SUMS | sha256sum -c -
